#====================================================================
# Draft: c-sig 3.8 device build - core.download:download_cache in
#        global.conf does NOT expand $HOME; silently ineffective and
#        conan falls back to a real download the device cannot reach
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-CSIG-DEVICE-DOWNLOAD-CACHE-ABS-PATH
trigger_tool:           conan
phase:                  source-download
error_signature:        Error downloading file.*timed out|HTTPSConnectionPool.*Connection to .* timed out|Error in source\(\) method

severity:               2
category:               conan-env-offline-cache
match_keywords:         download_cache, global.conf, core.download, $HOME, 绝对路径, absolute path, offline cache, sha256 pre-seed, GitHub 不可达, source(), 真机, isolated CONAN_HOME

title:                  conan global.conf 的 core.download:download_cache 不展开 $HOME — 必须写绝对路径，否则离线源码缓存静默失效并直连上游超时

root_cause:             Conan (verified 2.29.1-OHOS) treats [global.conf] values as literal strings: core.download:download_cache=$HOME/tmp/xx-dl creates a cache rooted at a directory literally named "$HOME", which never matches the pre-seeded <sha256[:2]>/<sha256> file, so conan silently attempts a real download; on a device without upstream egress (github.com connect timeout) source() then fails after retries with "Error downloading file ... timed out".
affected_scope:         Any device/isolated CONAN_HOME build that pre-seeds the sha256-keyed download cache to bypass blocked upstreams (the seeding method itself is E347); c-sig/3.8 on 10.62.134.118 is the delivered instance. Related trap in the same setup: the device's default ~/.conan2/profiles/ohos-aarch64 is stale (cppstd=gnu14, libstdc++, no compiler_executables) — always bring the repo CI profile instead of trusting the device default.
verification_cmd:       grep download_cache $CONAN_HOME/global.conf  # must show an absolute path, then rerun conan create

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           absolute-path-in-global-conf
rec_description:        Write the download cache with an absolute path: core.download:download_cache=/storage/Users/currentUser/tmp/<pkg>-dl (never $HOME or ~). Pre-seed the tarball as <cache>/<sha256[:2]>/<sha256>, verify with sha256sum on device. Then conan source() falls back to the cache after the first (expected) download timeout. Symptom pair to watch: one "WARN: network: Error downloading" followed by "Sources correctly downloaded from ..." = cache hit working; two timeouts + "Error in source() method" = cache path wrong.
rec_command:            printf 'core.download:download_cache=/storage/Users/currentUser/tmp/csig-dl\n' > $CONAN_HOME/global.conf
rec_auto_fix:           false
